    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408-a1">

                <pb facs="0478" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg418"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 305.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hanotaux to Mr. Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ambassador</hi>: By a letter dated March 21 last
                    the chargé d’affaires of the United States at Paris called my attention to
                    certain information which had reached his Government according to which the
                    resident general of the French Republic at Tunis had recently decided to
                    “suppress all the privileges, honors, and prerogatives granted to consuls by
                    treaties except those who were salaried officers.”</p>
                <p>I had not failed to interrogate our representative in the regency of Tunis with
                    reference to this matter, and I have just invited the ambassador of the French
                    Republic at Washington to furnish the Federal Government with such explanations
                    as appeared to me to be called for by Mr. Vignaud’s communication.</p>
                <pb facs="0479" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>
                <p>I deem it proper, however, to inform your excellency that the decision taken by
                    Mr. Réné Millet had only in view the withdrawal of the custom-house franchise
                    from the consular agents engaged in business.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Hanotaux</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
